# ══ research data — do not commit ═══════════════════════════════════════
# Human-subjects records from the wristband study: participant alcohol use,
# stress reports and continuous physiological recordings. Participant codes
# in these files are pseudonyms, not anonymisation. This data almost
# certainly sits under an IRB protocol and a data use agreement, so it stays
# local. The scripts that read it are committed; the data is not.
Alcohol Use Data/
Sensor Data/
Final Phone Survey Stress Events.xlsm
tlfb-transcribed.csv

# ══ binaries and build leftovers ════════════════════════════════════════
# The APK is a 4.6 MB debug-signed build. If you want to distribute it,
# attach it to a GitHub Release rather than committing it to the tree.
CraveCast.apk
*.bak

# ══ generated by the native build ══════════════════════════
# package.json, package-lock.json and capacitor.config.json ARE committed --
# CI clones this repo and has nothing else to go on. Everything below is
# reproduced from them by build-native.py and `npx cap add`, so committing it
# would only create two copies to keep in step.
node_modules/
www/
ios/
android/
build/

